{"id":"fbd296ec270b9a26895f42915a15860f3f48dcc3","axis":"silent","repo":"datafuselabs/databend","sha":"fbd296ec270b9a26895f42915a15860f3f48dcc3","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"Cargo.lock","lines":["@@ -5861,6 +5861,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"sha2 0.10.9\",","  \"socket2 0.5.9\",","  \"sqlx\",","+ \"subtle\",","  \"sysinfo\",","  \"temp-env\",","  \"tempfile\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -464,6 +464,7 @@ strength_reduce = \"0.2.4\""," stringslice = \"0.2.0\""," strum = \"0.24.1\""," sub-cache = \"0.2.1\"","+subtle = \"2.6.1\""," syn = { version = \"2.0\", features = [\"full\"] }"," sysinfo = \"0.34.2\""," tantivy = { version = \"0.26.2\", features = [\"quickwit\"] }"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/designs/http-query-token.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@","+# HTTP query-token authentication","+","+Tracking discussion: <https://github.com/databendlabs/databend/issues/21043>.","+","+## Protocol","+","+Submit SQL using existing Basic, JWT, key-pair or native session authentication.","+A created query returns an opaque token in `X-DATABEND-QUERY-TOKEN`, for both JSON","+and Arrow results. Neither the JSON body nor Arrow schema metadata contains a","+`query_token` field. Clients detect support by the response header; older clients","+may ignore it and continue using existing authentication.","+","+```http","+HTTP/1.1 200 OK","+X-DATABEND-QUERY-ID: <query-id>","+X-DATABEND-QUERY-TOKEN: <query-token>","+Cache-Control: no-store","+Access-Control-Expose-Headers: X-DATABEND-QUERY-ID, X-DATABEND-QUERY-TOKEN","+```","+","+Save the query ID and token before reading the response body. For follow-ups:","+","+```http","+GET /v1/query/<query-id>/page/1","+Authorization: Bearer <query-token>","+X-DATABEND-AUTH-METHOD: query-token","+```","+","+Query-token authentication is restricted to:","+","+| Method | Endpoint |","+| --- | --- |","+| GET | `/v1/query/:id` |","+| GET | `/v1/query/:id/page/:page_no` |","+| GET or POST | `/v1/query/:id/final` |","+| GET or POST | `/v1/query/:id/kill` |","+","+It cannot submit SQL, log in/out, refresh sessions, heartbeat, upload data or","+access metadata APIs. Session/temporary-table keepalive uses existing credentials;","+query-token requests do not refresh the client session's Meta handle.","+","+Only initial submission and eligible submission retries return the token header.","+State, page (including page zero/retries), final and kill never return it. An absent","+header on a follow-up must not clear the client's saved token.","+","+## Ownership, routing and retries","+","+The token is scoped to one query and its authenticated tenant/user. Request-body","+settings such as `sandbox_tenant` may change the execution tenant, not the owner.","+The route's query ID selects the query; `X-DATABEND-QUERY-ID` cannot override it.","+","+Retain existing routing headers. Sticky forwarding precedes token validation on","+the owning node; the expected-node header checks the destination, not ownership.","+In management mode, an explicit tenant header must match the owner. Otherwise,","+tenant headers follow the existing validation rules; headers ignored by Basic","+in sandbox-enabled configurations are also ignored by query-token authentication.","+An omitted tenant header is resolved from the validated query.","+","+If the query has a client session, every query-token follow-up requires its","+original cookie/session headers. Existing credentials may read state or kill a","+same-owner query across sessions, but page/final require the original session.","+","+A normally authenticated submission retry with the same client query ID may","+return the retained page zero for the same tenant/user. Only a matching original","+client session receives the token again. Another session may obtain the existing","+result without the token; it is not automatically switched to the original session.","+","+Losing the body after receiving headers still allows token-authenticated follow-ups.","+Losing the entire response does not guarantee recovery. If it established the first","+session, a retry may return page zero without restoring that session or its token.","+Establish a session before submission when reliable session-bound retries are","+needed. Do not automatically re-execute SQL when query state or its replayable","+response is lost; it may already have run.","+","+## Lifetime and errors","+","+Each query has a random 256-bit token, validated without user/policy/token lookups","+in Meta. New SQL still requires normal authentication and authorization. Tokens","+remain valid after the user's credentials change or the user is deleted; this is","+query-scoped access, not immediate per-request user revocation.","+","+There is no independent token TTL or refresh endpoint. The token lasts as long as","+the retained in-memory query record, including its closed retention period. It","+does not reopen closed result pages. Removal, expiry or node restart loses both","+query state and token; cross-node recovery and SQL replay are not provided.","+","+If initial page collection fails after registration, the server closes the new","+query and releases its result resources before returning the error, rather than","+leaving an active query without client credentials. This does not undo SQL that","+has already committed and is not a signal to automatically re-execute it.","+","+- Missing node-local query state returns **404**, not a reason to refresh credentials.","+- Invalid credentials, wrong tokens or ownership/session mismatches return **401**.","+- A query absent during ordinary authentication remains **404** if inserted before","+  the handler runs; that request must not access the newly inserted query.","+- Query-ID existence is not hidden: a wrong token for a retained query gives 401,","+  while a well-formed query-token request without retained query state gives 404.","+- Duplicate `X-DATABEND-AUTH-METHOD` headers are rejected on authenticated endpoints.","+","+## Transport and secrecy","+","+Use TLS. Never put tokens in URLs or unredacted logs/traces. Token-bearing responses","+use `Cache-Control: no-store`; server debug formatting and request-header logging","+redact tokens. Proxies/APM must independently redact `Authorization` and the new","+response header: an in-process sensitive flag does not travel over HTTP.","+","+The query server emits `Access-Control-Expose-Headers`, but does not enable CORS","+origins or credentials. Browser deployments must configure gateway/edge CORS and","+preserve exposure of both query headers. Header delivery alone does not establish","+safe caching, logging or cross-origin behavior."],"additions":110,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/common/base/src/headers.rs","lines":["@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ pub const HEADER_SESSION: &str = \"X-DATABEND-SESSION\";"," pub const HEADER_SESSION_ID: &str = \"X-DATABEND-SESSION-ID\";"," pub const HEADER_TENANT: &str = \"X-DATABEND-TENANT\";"," pub const HEADER_QUERY_ID: &str = \"X-DATABEND-QUERY-ID\";","+pub const HEADER_QUERY_TOKEN: &str = \"X-DATABEND-QUERY-TOKEN\";"," pub const HEADER_USER: &str = \"X-DATABEND-USER\";"," pub const HEADER_SQL: &str = \"X-DATABEND-SQL\";"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/query/service/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@ serde_stacker = { workspace = true }"," sha2 = { workspace = true }"," socket2 = { workspace = true }"," sqlx = { workspace = true }","+subtle = { workspace = true }"," sysinfo = { workspace = true }"," tempfile = { workspace = true }"," tokio = { workspace = true }"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/query/service/src/auth.rs","lines":["@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ pub struct AuthMgr {"," #[derive(Debug, Serialize)]"," pub enum CredentialType {","     DatabendToken,","+    QueryToken,","     Jwt,","     KeyPair,","     Password,","@@ -53,6 +54,10 @@ pub enum CredentialType {"," "," #[derive(Clone)]"," pub enum Credential {","+    QueryToken {","+        query_id: String,","+        token: String,","+    },","     DatabendToken {","         token: String,","     },","@@ -75,6 +80,7 @@ pub enum Credential {"," impl Credential {","     pub fn type_name(&self) -> CredentialType {","         match self {","+            Credential::QueryToken { .. } => CredentialType::QueryToken,","             Credential::DatabendToken { .. } => CredentialType::DatabendToken,","             Credential::Jwt { .. } => CredentialType::Jwt,","             Credential::KeyPair { .. } => CredentialType::KeyPair,","@@ -85,6 +91,7 @@ impl Credential {"," ","     pub fn user_name(&self) -> Option<String> {","         match self {","+            Credential::QueryToken { .. } => None,","             Credential::DatabendToken { .. } => None,","             Credential::Jwt { .. } => None,","             Credential::KeyPair { .. } => None,","@@ -124,6 +131,11 @@ impl AuthMgr {","             .unwrap_or_default();","         match credential {","             Credential::NoNeed => Ok((\"\".to_string(), None)),","+            // HTTP middleware authorizes query capabilities against a specific","+            // query object. They must never initialize ordinary SQL privileges.","+            Credential::QueryToken { .. } => Err(ErrorCode::AuthenticateFailure(","+                \"Query tokens require HTTP query authorization\",","+            )),","             Credential::DatabendToken { token } => {","                 let claim = ClientSessionManager::instance().verify_token(token).await?;","                 let tenant = Tenant::new_or_err(claim.tenant.to_string(), func_name!())?;"],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/query/service/src/servers/http/middleware/session.rs","lines":["@@ -19,11 +19,13 @@ use std::collections::HashMap;"," use std::sync::Arc;"," "," use databend_common_base::base::GlobalInstance;","+use databend_common_base::headers::HEADER_AUTH_METHOD;"," use databend_